{"id": "EUVD-2026-81040", "enisaUuid": "9edec503-676e-3195-a1e3-214c273b6c8d", "description": "Wiki.js through 2.5.314 fails to require path separators when matching START and END page rules, allowing attackers to access pages sharing a prefix with authorized folders. Users granted access to a folder can read and modify unrelated pages with matching prefixes, bypassing intended access controls.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T20:32:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-18T18:32:42", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/geo-chen/oss/blob/main/wiki.md#finding-3-page-permission-rule-engine-grants-readwrite-access-to-any-page-whose-path-shares-a-literal-prefix-with-an-allowed-path-no-path-segment-boundary-check", "https://github.com/requarks/wiki/blob/v2.5.314/server/core/auth.js#L252-L263", "https://github.com/requarks/wiki", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wiki-js-through-2.5.314-path-prefix-matching-authorization-bypass"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mxgr-89mh-cjg6", "CVE-2026-92776"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "47a1b520-f3a8-3dec-bee0-0436e2a7ee17", "product": {"name": "Wiki.js", "vendor": {"name": "Requarks.io"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.5.314"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ece74d05-bd3d-3f10-9133-ab54ba13361d", "vendor": {"name": "Requarks"}}], "isExploited": false}